---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { company } from '../content/company';
---

<Prose title="Terms of use" eyebrow="The small print" description="The terms for using the Lorapay website and joining its waitlist." updated={company.policyDate}>
  <p class="lead">
    These terms cover this website and the Lorapay waitlist, provided by {company.legalName} (RC {company.rcNumber}). Using the
    Lorapay app will be covered by separate terms when it launches.
  </p>

  <h2>Lorapay is not open yet</h2>
  <p>
    This website describes a service that is still being built. It does not offer payment, banking or any other financial
    service, and nothing on it is financial advice. Features, limits and launch dates may change before launch.
    When Lorapay opens, customer money will be held through Anchor (Anchor Technologies) and its licensed partner banks, not by
    {company.legalName}.
  </p>

  <h2>The waitlist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Joining is free and doesn't oblige you to use Lorapay.</li>
    <li>Joining doesn't guarantee access on any date, or at all. We may open by state, in stages, or by invitation.</li>
    <li>Please give your own, accurate details. You must be 18 or older.</li>
    <li>You can leave at any time by emailing <a href={`mailto:${company.privacyEmail}`}>{company.privacyEmail}</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>How we handle your details is explained in our <a href="/privacy">website privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <p>Please don't misuse the site: no attempts to break or overload it, no automated sign-ups, and no false or other people's details.</p>
  <p>Security research is welcome under the rules on our <a href="/security#report">security page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The Lorapay name, logo, designs and text on this site belong to {company.legalName}. You may share links to the site, but
    please don't copy our branding or present yourself as Lorapay.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep this site accurate and available, but we provide it "as is". To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable
    for losses arising from using it or relying on it. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't be limited under
    Nigerian law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and law</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version. These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal
    Republic of Nigeria, and the courts of Lagos State have jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> · {company.address}</p>
</Prose>
